# Home Base UI

- Primary viewport is still iPhone Safari over VPN; also keep desktop readable (wider max widths, clear contrast).
- Bottom tabs: Apps · Shell · Files · Cursor · Logs · Alerts · Settings.
- Share / password live under **Settings** (localhost only), not a separate tab.
- Shell = interactive PTY + session attach (former Mon). Logs = capped console ring (300).
- Workspace pickers and Run stacks use native `<select>` dropdowns (`hb-select`).
- Ship actions are hold-to-confirm; Run/Stop is a toggle from port/session state.
- Pull-to-refresh is global (top-of-scroll drag).
- Theme: night (default) + day via `data-theme` / Settings; Syne + IBM Plex Mono; teal accent. Avoid purple gradients and cream/serif clichés.
- New/Add actions use compact `IconBtn` (`+`), not text labels.
- Layout tokens: `.hb-page`, `.hb-chrome`, `.hb-surface`, floating `.hb-nav` dock with icons + labels; safe-area padding for iPhone.
- Breakpoints: phone-first; iPad (`md`) wider chrome; desktop (`lg`) two-column Apps where useful.
- Shell tab must remain usable with on-screen Ctrl/Esc helpers.
- Cursor tab streams markdown; show project cwd and agent id.
